jobs.description:
Are you technically minded and do you enjoy working with precision? Would you like to work with aviation safety equipment used by major international airlines? And are you looking for a long-term career with the possibility of a direct contract? Then this Technical Employee position in Duiven could be the perfect opportunity for you!

What are you going to do?
In this role, you will work with safety equipment used in aircraft. Your job is to inspect, test and maintain critical aviation safety products according to strict technical manuals. You will always follow detailed English instructions and procedures. Precision and accuracy are extremely important, because the equipment you work with plays a vital role in passenger safety. You will work closely with colleagues from different departments and register your work in the internal system.

Your tasks include:

- Performing inspections on aviation safety equipment such as evacuation slides;
- Testing products by inflating, pressure testing and checking for leaks or defects;
- Carefully following detailed English technical manuals and safety procedures;
- Documenting inspections and results in the company system (Quantum);
- Communicating with colleagues from customer service and other departments;
- Identifying and reporting any irregularities immediately.

This is a full-time position (40 hours) from Monday to Friday, 07:00 – 16:00. In the future, the company may transition to a two-shift system, so flexibility is important.

What do we offer?
- You will be hired directly by the company;
- Salary between €2,900 and €3,600 gross per month;
- A bonus plan;
- Extensive training program of 2–6 months depending on the department;
- Opportunity to learn multiple departments and become multi-skilled;
- Travel allowance;
- A close-knit team with short communication lines;
- Stable long-term career opportunities in the aviation industry.

